{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1159759-help-with-clues","id":1159759,"title":"Help with clues","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-17T03:07:13-08:00","id":1159759,"title":"Help with clues","content":"So I'm running a Chronicles of Darkness game. I'm a relative veteran of it (I've run them regularly for a few years), but did it almost entirely pre-2nd edition or otherwise ignoring the new core rules -- doors, chases, and clues, primarily. <br /> <br /> My new game is somewhat centered around a series of murders, and to spare the details, someone's being framed. In a particular scene, there's a several damning items found in a the trunk of someone's car (it's part of the frame) and a player wants to roll Investigation to uncover a clue. What's the best way to handle giving them that? <br /> <br /> Honestly, any help with Clues would be amazing. I'm somewhat vexed by them in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T07:16:21-08:00","id":1159829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1159759-help-with-clues#post1159759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm running a Chronicles of Darkness game. I'm a relative veteran of it (I've run them regularly for a few years), but did it almost entirely pre-2nd edition or otherwise ignoring the new core rules -- doors, chases, and clues, primarily.<br /> <br /> My new game is somewhat centered around a series of murders, and to spare the details, someone's being framed. In a particular scene, there's a several damning items found in a the trunk of someone's car (it's part of the frame) and a player wants to roll Investigation to uncover a clue. What's the best way to handle giving them that?<br /> <br /> Honestly, any help with Clues would be amazing. I'm somewhat vexed by them in general.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, obviously, the most basic clue is the framer left behind something of his in the car, a piece of evidence that points to A. that the framer exists and is aware of the players. and B. the framer's identity.<br /> <br /> The second part is where things get interesting, because depending on who the killer is, the nature of what the clue is changes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Even as something as basic as DNA evidence from hair rules out whether or not the perpatrator is even <i>human </i>if the basic genome found doesn't match any of the protiens you would expect in a human gene sample.<br /> <br /> Flecks of paint and scraps of sawdust meanwhile can hint someone who is tied towards construction.<br /> <br /> <br /> Unless you mean Clues rules...and not clue examples...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 11-17-2017, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T11:34:03-08:00","id":1159935,"title":"","content":"In the new investigation rules, characters roll to discover clues, which can then help them solve the case and be used for bonuses on related things. Each clue comes with &quot;elements&quot; which are essentially its number of uses.<br /> Succeed on an investigaton roll (with any relevant skill), you get a clue with 1 element/use. Add one if exceptional success. Add 1 if their skill rating is 4+ dots. Add 1 if they have a relevent specialty. And there are merits that can help.<br /> You're supposed to save 1 use from every major clue to solve the crime. All those extra uses become discretionary dice, letting them add +1 to rolls to find more clues, pursue leads, or subdue the criminal - anything related to the investigation, basically.<br /> <br /> If they fail a roll, you can give the clue a &quot;tag&quot; (a flaw) that complicates the investigation. Maybe the find prints, but they match several potential suspects, for example.<br /> <br /> Players can use the elements their supposed to save up if they really need to, but if they don't have 1 per major clue by the end, the villain gets benefits - like being prepared, or getting away, or getting a mistrial.<br /> <br /> <br /> The new investigation system looks complex on a first read, but I've found it actually works pretty well. I write up clues on notecards, drawing in a box for each element and noting any tags. That way everyone can visually keep track of the investigation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T15:13:25-08:00","id":1160327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1159759-help-with-clues?p=1159935#post1159935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the new investigation rules, characters roll to discover clues, which can then help them solve the case and be used for bonuses on related things. Each clue comes with &quot;elements&quot; which are essentially its number of uses.<br /> Succeed on an investigaton roll (with any relevant skill), you get a clue with 1 element/use. Add one if exceptional success. Add 1 if their skill rating is 4+ dots. Add 1 if they have a relevent specialty. And there are merits that can help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notably, you do this on a failed roll too. The only difference is that it comes with either the Incomplete or Tainted tag, which modify the effects of its elements.<br /> <br /> The thing to take away here is that players can\u2019t miss Clues. The roll only serves to determine how effectively they will be able to use the Clue they find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T05:04:19-08:00","id":1160814,"title":"","content":"I created with <b>MrGone</b> a Clues Cards, to make easier managing them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/NWOD/CofD_ClueCards_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/p...nteractive.pdf</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}